<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><rss xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" version="2.0"><channel><title>India News | Latest India News Today &amp; Real-time News from India, India Breaking News</title><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india</link><description>India News Today: Get latest India news and breaking news from India on Times of India. TOI brings the top news headlines from India on Politics, Elections, Current Affairs and more</description><language>en-gb</language><lastBuildDate>2026-10-06T19:35:40+05:30</lastBuildDate><atom:link type="application/rss+xml" rel="self" href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/rssfeeds/-2128936835.cms"/><copyright>Copyright:(C) Tue, 06 Oct 2026 19:35:40 IST Bennett Coleman &amp; Co. Ltd, http://in.indiatimes.com/policyterms/1554651.cms</copyright><docs>http://syndication.indiatimes.com/</docs><image><title>India News | Latest India News Today &amp; Real-time News from India, India Breaking News</title><url>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/507610.cms</url><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india</link></image><item><title><![CDATA['No meeting request received from any party': EC officials as Rahul, Priyanka refuse to leave 'protest site']]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/no-meeting-request-received-from-any-party-ec-officials-as-rahul-priyanka-refuse-to-leave-protest-site/articleshow/134741393.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134741393.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Congress leaders Rahul Gandhi and Priyanka Gandhi Vadra staged a protest near the Election Commission's office, even as the EC said it had received no request from any political party seeking a meeting. Cong said they demanded a meeting to discuss alleged electoral irregularities and questioned Chief Election Commissioner Gyanesh Kumar. The police intervened and detained several opposition leaders as the protest escalated.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/no-meeting-request-received-from-any-party-ec-officials-as-rahul-priyanka-refuse-to-leave-protest-site/articleshow/134741393.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/no-meeting-request-received-from-any-party-ec-officials-as-rahul-priyanka-refuse-to-leave-protest-site/articleshow/134741393.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-06T18:39:47+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Kanchan Yadav</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134741646,imgsize-130152.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[The India mood: Confidence in the country, anxiety about careers]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/the-india-mood-confidence-in-the-country-anxiety-about-careers/articleshow/134740782.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134740782.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[India leads in consumer confidence, yet respondents express significant worries about unemployment and education quality. Many Indians believe the country is on the right track, despite job market uncertainties. The disconnect between economic optimism and job security highlights ongoing issues affecting connected consumers.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/the-india-mood-confidence-in-the-country-anxiety-about-careers/articleshow/134740782.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/the-india-mood-confidence-in-the-country-anxiety-about-careers/articleshow/134740782.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-06T18:24:46+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Arghya Prasun Roychowdhury</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134741001,imgsize-2089738.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Jharkhand protest: Congress workers scuffle with police outside CEO office]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/jharkhand-protest-congress-workers-scuffle-with-police-outside-ceo-office/articleshow/134740655.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134740655.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[In Ranchi, Congress workers in Jharkhand rallied outside the Chief Electoral Officer's office to protest against Gyanesh Kumar. The demonstration escalated as protestors clashed with police while attempting to breach barriers and defaced the commission's nameplate. Their aim was to draw attention to the challenges citizens face with the electoral roll.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/jharkhand-protest-congress-workers-scuffle-with-police-outside-ceo-office/articleshow/134740655.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/jharkhand-protest-congress-workers-scuffle-with-police-outside-ceo-office/articleshow/134740655.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-06T18:09:52+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Mahima Sharma</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134740897,imgsize-156344.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Once a skunk, always a skunk': DMK questions Rahul Gandhi's stand on Tamil Nadu SIR deletions amid anti-CEC protest]]></title><description><![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/once-a-skunk-always-a-skunk-dmk-questions-rahul-gandhis-stand-on-tamil-nadu-sir-deletions-amid-anti-cec-protest/articleshow/134739393.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/once-a-skunk-always-a-skunk-dmk-questions-rahul-gandhis-stand-on-tamil-nadu-sir-deletions-amid-anti-cec-protest/articleshow/134739393.cms]]></guid><pubD